    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the specifics. I\'m focusing on dissecting the request, ensuring I understand every nuance of this Kazakh-language interactive educational web app, focusing on the title\'s implications and how it suggests the best way to approach the work. I\'m concentrating on the requirements for the user interface text.\n\n\n**Defining the App\'s Aesthetic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual style. I\'m imagining a \"mystical, mysterious, modern\" look, centering on deep navy, purple, and neon-cyan, with glowing gold highlights and smooth animations. The top section needs to display the app\'s title and concise instructions in Kazakh, as well as a central table block.\n\n\n**Formulating the Interaction**\n\nI\'m now crafting the interactive elements. I\'m focusing on the \"\320\234\320\265\320\275\321\226\322\243 \321\201\320\260\320\275\321\213\320\274 \320\276\321\201\321\213\320\275\320\264\320\260\" toggle buttons for each column, visualizing the neon glow and borders on selection. I\'m also considering the \"\322\232\322\261\320\277\320\270\321\217\320\275\321\213 \320\260\321\210\321\203\" mode and how to unveil the hidden keys subtly. I\'m also planning the placement of the \"\320\241\320\260\320\275\320\264\321\213 \320\261\321\226\320\273\321\203 \342\234\250\" and \"\322\232\320\260\320\271\321\202\320\260 \320\261\320\260\321\201\321\202\320\260\321\203 \360\237\224\204\" buttons. I\'m thinking about the flow for the \"\320\222\320\270\321\200\321\202\321\203\320\260\320\273\320\264\321\213 \320\241\320\270\322\233\321\213\321\200\321\210\321\213\" chat window, its typing effect, and its function.\n\nI\'ve also specified the scenario for Step 1 (reveal result).\n\n\n**Elaborating the Flow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user\'s journey. I\'ve broken the process into steps: the initial prompt if no column is selected, then the secret revelation with the \"\320\230\323\231, \322\233\322\261\320\277\320\270\321\217\321\201\321\213\320\275 \320\260\321\210!\" button. Following that, the explanation with the key numbers and formula reveal, linking it back to powers of 2 and binary. I\'m imagining how the \"\320\222\320\270\321\200\321\202\321\203\320\260\320\273\320\264\321\213 \320\241\320\270\322\233\321\213\321\200\321\210\321\213\" chat will communicate all this engagingly in Kazakh. The Q&A is being worked on.\n\n\n"
