  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Setup**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing `metadata.json` and `index.html`. It looks like `express` and `tsx` are pre-installed, which is a good sign. React guidelines suggest using a `server.ts` entry point with Express and `vite.middlewares` for development environments; this aligns with the installed tools. I\'m focusing on how these components integrate within the existing setup.\n\n\n**Confirming Server Integration**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `server.ts` handles the backend routes with Express, as the docs stipulate. This fits seamlessly, especially given `vite.middlewares` for development and the planned `server.ts` entry point with `tsx`. The Gemini API route is now confirmed to be handled by `server.ts`. Moreover, I\'ve checked the `@google/genai` version, which is 2.4.0, meeting the minimum requirement.\n\n\n**Verifying Package Installation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring the `@google/genai` package is at the right version. I\'m verifying this and plan to update it to the latest version. I\'ll test it out or install with `install_applet_package`, to ensure it is handled safely.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m also shifting gears to updating the project\'s metadata. I\'m going to fill in the missing `name` and `description` fields in `metadata.json`. The name will be \"\320\241\320\270\322\233\321\213\321\200\320\273\321\213 \320\272\320\265\321\201\321\202\320\265 \342\200\224 \320\234\320\260\320\263\320\270\321\217\320\273\321\213\322\233 \320\274\320\260\321\202\320\265\320\274\320\260\321\202\320\270\320\272\320\260\320\273\321\213\322\233 \321\204\320\276\320\272\321\203\321\201\" and the description will be \"1 \320\274\320\265\320\275 31 \320\260\321\200\320\260\320\273\321\213\322\223\321\213\320\275\320\264\320\260\322\223\321\213 \321\201\320\260\320\275\320\264\321\213 \321\202\320\260\320\261\320\260\321\202\321\213\320\275 \320\265\320\272\321\226\320\273\321\226\320\272 \321\201\320\260\320\275\320\260\321\203 \320\266\322\257\320\271\320\265\321\201\321\226\320\275\320\265 \320\275\320\265\320\263\321\226\320\267\320\264\320\265\320\273\320\263\320\265\320\275 \320\270\320\275\321\202\320\265\321\200\320\260\320\272\321\202\320\270\320\262\321\202\321\226 \321\201\320\270\322\233\321\213\321\200\320\273\321\213 \320\272\320\265\321\201\321\202\320\265 \320\266\323\231\320\275\320\265 \320\262\320\270\321\200\321\202\321\203\320\260\320\273\320\264\321\213 \321\201\320\270\322\233\321\213\321\200\321\210\321\213 \320\226\320\230 \320\272\323\251\320\274\320\265\320\272\321\210\321\226\321\201\321\226.\" I also see that the `<title>` tag in `index.html` is consistent.\n\n\n**Defining Ultra Mode Journeys**\n\nI\'m now outlining the \"Ultra Mode\" user journeys, specifically Journey 1, where the user thinks of a number and clicks corresponding columns, followed by the magician\'s reveal with an animation. Journey 2 involves the user choosing to reveal the magic\'s mechanics, explaining the underlying binary system and the \"hidden keys.\" I\'m determining if and how the journeys will trigger the visual and auditory effects.\n\n\n**Elaborating Feature Journeys**\n\nI\'m expanding the \"Ultra Mode\" user journeys further. Journey 3 will involve a magician chat where users ask questions in Kazakh; this leverages Gemini 3.8 Flash, but includes a local fallback for instant answers. Journey 4 introduces an \"Interactive Number Trainer\" to visually demonstrate binary decomposition. Journey 5 then offers a reset, restarting the interactive magic.\n\n\n**Implementing Math Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the core logic for the magic table. I\'m writing pure math functions in `src/utils/magicTable.ts`, which includes key functions such as `calculateGuessedNumber`, `getColumnsForNumber`, `getBinaryString`, and `getMathematicalFormula`. This will involve a suite of unit tests in `test/magicTable.test.ts` to ensure everything functions properly, including testing edge cases and invalid inputs. I\'ll make sure to verify the `@google/genai` package version is up to date, and upgrade it if needed.\n\n\n"
