  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating Dependencies & Scripts**\n\nI\'ve just bumped `@google/genai` to version `^2.32.0`. I\'m also planning to adjust the `package.json` scripts. Specifically, I intend to set `\"dev\"` to `\"tsx server.ts\"` and `\"start\"` to either `\"node server.js\"` or `\"tsx server.ts\"`. This should allow full-stack Express and Vite middleware to function properly with our Gemini API.\n\n\n**Verifying Server Setup**\n\nI\'m now confirming the `server.ts` setup aligns with React guidelines, specifically the full-stack pattern. This confirms the plan to use `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` and `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"` in `package.json`. The `server.ts` will establish an Express app with `express.json()` and the `/api/magician/chat` endpoint. This endpoint will receive specific data and initialize `GoogleGenAI` with the Gemini API key, using `gemini-3.8-flash` and a system prompt.\n\n\n**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enhanced error management. My plan involves a robust fallback mechanism in Kazakh. If the `GEMINI_API_KEY` is absent or the Gemini API call fails, I\'ll generate a tailored, informative response to explain concepts like binary representation and powers of two in a clear and engaging manner. This ensures users receive valuable information even when the primary API is unavailable.\n\n\n"
